 "notes": "The catalogue lists Balabhadra as the scribe. That is wrong: the colophon says Vaṭukanātha (written vaṭuknātho(!)), grandson of Balabhadra, did the copying. 'sudhīḥ' is a praise word for the scribe, not a title. 'santosa' stands for santoṣa. The colophon has no date. Mahārāja Rājendra is probably Rājendra Vikrama Śāha of Nepal (r. 1816–1847), but the colophon gives only 'Rājendra', so this is not certain.",
